// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// charToUnicode(char)  -  NOT USED, unfinished
//
// Nothing in the project calls this (checked: no other script or object event
// mentions it). It only knows "A" (65) and "B" (66) and returns nothing for
// anything else. The built-in ord() does the whole job. Safe to ignore.
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
function charToUnicode(argument0) {
	if argument0=="A" return 65;
	if argument0=="B" return 66;


}
